{"name":"Mustang","hex":"#5e4a47","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"Mustang","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An American sports car, manufactured by Ford Motor Company from 1964 till present, a cultural icon and the longest-produced Ford nameplate.","The P-51 Mustang was a single-seat fighter plane designed by North American Aviation in 1940."]},{"part":"Proper noun","definitions":["A district of Nepal.","A place in the United States:\nA city in Canadian County, Oklahoma. \nA town in Navarro County, Texas. It has no population."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Mustang"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mustang","blocks":[{"text":"The mustang is a free-roaming horse of the Western United States, descended from horses brought to the Americas by the Spanish conquistadors. Mustangs are often referred to as wild horses, but because they descend from domesticated stock, they are formally classified as feral horses. The original mustangs were Colonial Spanish horses, but many other breeds and types of horses contributed to the modern mustang, now resulting in varying phenotypes. Some free-roaming horses are relatively unchanged from the original Spanish stock, most strongly represented in the most isolated populations."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/de/Mustanggelding.jpg/330px-Mustanggelding.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mustang","wikidata":"Q211848"},{"title":"Mustang (military officer)","blocks":[{"text":"Mustang is a military slang term used in the United States Armed Forces to refer to a commissioned officer who began their career as an enlisted service member. A mustang officer is not a temporary or brevet promotion but is a commissioned officer who receives more pay according to their rank of O1-E, O2-E, etc., but has no more command responsibilities than those of any commissioned officer of the same grade."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mustang_(military_officer)","wikidata":"Q6943390"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg/500px-Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg/1280px-Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9d/Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg/500px-Arizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArizona_2004_Mustangs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Horsescd1l-095.jpg/500px-Horsescd1l-095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/24/Horsescd1l-095.jpg/500px-Horsescd1l-095.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Mustang mare and foal with stallion in the West Warm Springs HMA (Herd Management Area) in Oregon","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AHorsescd1l-095.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Mustang_Utah_2005_2.jpg/500px-Mustang_Utah_2005_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e0/Mustang_Utah_2005_2.jpg/500px-Mustang_Utah_2005_2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Large herd of free-roaming mustangs galloping through the plains of Utah","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMustang_Utah_2005_2.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/fe/Comancheria.jpg/500px-Comancheria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_cont